# knit's osc 2 fine tune (TP_O2FINE, a tester: "OSC2 Fine Tune instead of Semitones"): on the Osc 2 page, knob 2,
# beside osc 2's interval (it was HOME held on Sub's osc 2 knob until the page came: tests/scenarios/osc2page.xy), in
# cents (+-50). Kept over a restart; a factory preset sets it back to 0; a user preset keeps it
wait 300
spin ALGO 2
expect trk 3
knob 3 engine knit
tap EDIT
turn SELECT 1
expect page Osc_2
spin K1 7
expect par3.x1 71
expect par3.fine 64
listen
spin K2 12
wait 400
said fine +12 ct
shot fine_page.png
spin K2 60
expect par3.fine 114
spin K2 -88
expect par3.fine 26
spin K2 14
wait 40
expect par3.fine 40
expect par3.x1 71
spin K1 1
expect par3.x1 72
expect par3.fine 40
expect epar3.fine 40
projsave 1
reboot
wait 400
expect par3.fine 40
expect par3.x1 72
# a factory preset: no fine tune
preset 3 reese
expect par3.fine 64
# a user preset keeps it, also over a restart (presets format 8)
knob 3 x1 70
knob 3 fine 90
usersave 3 2
preset 3 reese
expect par3.fine 64
reboot
wait 400
preset 3 U2
expect par3.fine 90
expect par3.x1 70
# user presets saved in format 7 (tests/fixtures/make_presets_v7.xy) load, each at no fine tune
storeload tests/fixtures/store_presets_v7.bin
reboot
wait 400
preset 3 U1
expect par3.engine 0
expect par3.x1 75
expect par3.x2 90
expect par3.fine 64
# breaks-out's format 8 (tests/fixtures/make_presets_v8.py: the user presets without the fine, then the user kits)
# put back: U1 at no fine tune, kit K1 there (its keys on two removed models: a kick and a snare from their defaults);
# loading a kit leaves the track's fine as it was
restore tests/fixtures/presets_v8.bkp
expect restore_rc 0
wait 400
preset 3 U1
expect par3.x1 75
expect par3.x2 90
expect par3.fine 64
expect trk 1
param 1 fine 77
tap EDIT
expect page Engine
tap SEL
row KIT
turn ALGO -8
tap SEL
wait 40
expect par1.d1.model 0
expect par1.d1.k1 82
expect par1.d1.k5 0
expect par1.d2.model 1
expect par1.fine 77
# a kit saved (now format 11, eight kits after the presets with their fine), Loom loaded, the kit back: its keys (a key
# on sophie, model 20: a development build's number before format 10, a model of its own now: kept)
param 1 d3.model 4
param 1 d5.model 20
tap SEL
row SAVE KIT
turn ALGO 1
tap SEL
wait 40
expect ask 0
tap SEL
row KIT
turn ALGO 8
tap SEL
wait 40
expect par1.d3.model 2
tap SEL
row KIT
turn ALGO -7
tap SEL
wait 40
expect par1.d3.model 4
expect par1.d5.model 20
expect par1.d2.model 1
expect par1.fine 77
# the project saved (format 17): the key on sophie stays sophie after a reboot
tap SAVE
wait 40
reboot
wait 400
expect par1.d5.model 20
preset 3 U1
expect par3.x1 75
expect par3.fine 64
